{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-104671",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the radical as a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{9}}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{7}}}=\\frac{{y}^{9}}{{({y}^{7})}^{1/3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we apply the power rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{9}}{{({y}^{7})}^{1/3}}=\\frac{{y}^{9}}{{y}^{7(1/3)}}=\\frac{{y}^{9}}{{y}^{7/3}}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{9}}{{y}^{7/3}} & = \\\\ {y}^{9-7/3} & = \\\\ {y}^{20/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we express the result as a radical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{20/3} & =\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{20}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
